{"object":"Occupation","stdCode":"OCC0314","name":"Public service operational delivery officer","status":1,"statusName":"Approved occupation","level":3,"versionNo":"1.1","statusLastUpdated":"2015-08-27","summary":"Operational Delivery Officers have the vital job of keeping the country running. They make sure that citizens get the services and protection they need, and help people understand what is available and what they need to do to comply with the rules. Operational Delivery Officers make a difference every day to the lives of millions of people. They do hundreds of jobs in most departments and agencies in central government. They also work in local government, delivering services for towns, cities, boroughs or counties.\n\nThis apprenticeship will give you great development opportunities to equip you to be an internationally-recognised professional in the part of the Civil Service that really makes things happen for customers and businesses.\n","overview":"Working in local and central government to ensure the public gets the services and protection they need","involvedEmployers":"Department for Work and Pensions, HMRC, Home Office, Department for Transport, Ministry of Justice, Kent County Council","keywords":["government","operational","operational delivery","protection","public services"],"soc":{"soc2010Code":4112,"soc2010Description":"National government administrative occupations","soc2020Code":4111,"soc2020Description":"National government administrative occupations","soc2020SubUnitGroups":[{"code":"4111/99","description":"National government administrative occupations n.e.c.","isPrimary":true}]},"mapHierarchy":{"routeId":2,"routeName":"Business and administration","routeSequence":1,"pathwayId":19,"pathwayName":"Management and Administration","clusterGroupId":64,"clusterId":45,"clusterName":"Administrator","technicalLevel":1,"technicalLevelName":"Technical","pathwaySequence":1,"clusterGroupSequence":0,"clusterSeqeunce":0},"products":[{"object":"Product","n